Patch 2035: d3d12: branch-free 16-bit index pass in upload_vpull (VPULL_FAST16); FP_SHOW on MRT programs

Source: that port's toolkit a1e4795.

- upload_vpull: the common case (16-bit indices, no restart, no strip prefix)
  reads indices and their range in a straight loop; the general loop re-tested
  width, restart and prefix per index. Render thread upload_vpull exclusive in
  battle: 22% in the maintainer's burst profile, 6.5% in px1 (with SRV_SKIP and the
  AVX2 builds). VPULL_FAST16=0 off.
- FP_SHOW=<expr> also replaces '_out.t0 = ' in multiple-render-target programs
  (that port's unit materials write t0-t3).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index c31a4be7..2fc62442 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
